Gamification on the client
=========================

The server owns the rules. This file describes how the client presents them
and which numbers it is allowed to compute.

The one rule that matters: the app displays what the API sends. It does not
recompute XP curves, streaks or tiers. Where a constant appears on both sides
it is a mirror, and mirrors are listed at the bottom of this file so they can
be changed together.


XP and level
------------

GET /user/me returns totalXp, level, xpIntoLevel, xpMax and xpToNext. The
Lancer level card on HomeScreen renders all five directly:

	LANCER LEVEL <level>
	<tier name> - Tier <sub rank>
	<xpIntoLevel> / <xpMax> XP        <xpToNext> to next

The progress bar is xpIntoLevel / xpMax. If the server changes the curve the
card follows without a client release.

Level up is detected by AppContext comparing the level it last saw against the
level in a fresh profile response. A change raises LevelUpModal. Nothing else
in the app triggers that modal.


Tiers and avatars
-----------------

Five tiers, mirrored from the backend in src/data/facultyTheme.js:

	Tier 1  Squire   levels 1-2
	Tier 2  Knight   levels 3-7
	Tier 3  Hero     levels 8-13
	Tier 4  Legend   levels 14-19
	Tier 5  Lancer   levels 20-25

	tierForLevel(level)    the tier index
	tierName(level)        the display name
	getAvatarSource(facultyKey, level)   the art for that faculty and tier

Art changes only at a tier boundary. There are five images per faculty, not
twenty-five. Sub-levels reuse the tier's art and are shown as rank pips, which
is the intended behaviour and not a missing asset.

The faculty key comes from the backend serializer as facultyKey. The client
never derives it from the faculty display string.

FacultyAvatar.js selects the image; KnightAvatar.js is the SVG fallback when
no faculty key is available.


AvatarJourneyScreen
-------------------

The progression map, reached from ProfileScreen.

Five floating islands on a starlit field, one per tier, threaded bottom to top
by a single winding trail. Each stop shows the tier's real avatar art, the
levels it covers, and the XP required to unlock it.

	current tier    gold star, "You are here"
	cleared tiers   check mark
	locked tiers    frosted scrim plus a lock glyph, still visible

Locked tiers stay visible on purpose. A student needs to see what they are
working toward; hiding it removes the reason to keep going.

Medallions are absolutely positioned against a fixed virtual canvas scaled to
the screen width, so the stops stay locked to the terrain at any device size.
The SVG is rendered at real pixel size with a viewBox rather than scaled with
a CSS transform, which blurs it.


Streak
------

The streak comes from /user/me and is derived server side from the distinct
days the student logged an activity. A streak survives until midnight even if
today has no session yet, so the flame does not disappear at 00:01 on a day
the student is still going to train.

The client displays the number and the loggedToday flag. It does not count
days itself.


Daily quests
------------

Three quests per day, fetched from GET /quest/daily. HomeScreen shows them
with progress and a claim button; the Challenges screen links to the full set.

The rotation is decided by the server. Staff can pin a specific set for a
date, otherwise a deterministic pick from the bank applies. The client is not
aware of which of the two produced today's list, and should not become aware.

Claiming posts to POST /quest/:id/claim and then refetches the profile so the
new XP total and any level change land through the normal path.

The claim endpoint currently has no completion record and no idempotency
guard. The client must not be relied on to prevent double claims. See the
backend's docs/maintenance.md.


Challenges
----------

	browse      GET /challenge/active, including recentParticipants so cards
	            show real joiner avatars
	join        POST /challenge/:id/register
	board       GET /challenge/:id/leaderboard
	log result  POST /challenge/:id/submit-points

Per-challenge status lives in AppContext as pending, submitted, approved or
rejected. The challenge sheet's call to action follows that status: join,
then log a result, then awaiting review, then log another result once a
decision has been made. Re-submission after approval or rejection is allowed
by the backend and the sheet exposes it.

Supervised challenges are validated in person by TLC staff. The app's job
ends at submission; approval happens in the admin console and comes back as a
validation:decided socket event plus a push notification.


Badges
------

	catalogue   GET /badge/all
	earned      GET /badge/me

BadgesScreen shows both, with unearned badges dimmed rather than hidden.
AppContext keeps a badgeQueue of newly awarded badges; BadgeAwardModal drains
it one at a time so two badges earned in one action do not collide.

Badge XP is already included in totalXp by the time the client sees it. The
modal celebrates, it does not add.


Check-in
--------

Worth 75 XP, once per calendar day, POST /checkin.

hooks/useGymProximity.js watches location and prompts on a rising edge into
the TLC radius, once per crossing rather than continuously. The prompt is
gated on the auto check-in setting, so a student who turned it off is not
asked. The manual button on HomeScreen always works regardless of the setting.


Steps
-----

hooks/usePedometer.js reads real step data through expo-sensors and builds the
weekly history. Steps are shown on HomeScreen and LogScreen against a goal.
They are a display metric; they do not award XP.


Mirrors to keep in sync
-----------------------

Each of these exists here and in the backend. Change both or neither.

	XP per level, 2000
	    here: implied by xpMax from the API, no local constant
	    backend: meController.levelFromXp and utils/serializers.levelFromXp

	Tier boundaries 1 / 3 / 8 / 14 / 20
	    here: src/data/facultyTheme.js tierForLevel
	    backend: utils/serializers.avatarTierFromLevel

	Faculty keys faculty1..faculty9
	    here: src/data/facultyTheme.js, avatarSources.js,
	          facultyBadgeSources.js, and the asset folder names
	    backend: FACULTY_KEY_BY_VALUE in utils/serializers.ts

	Check-in value 75 XP
	    here: display copy only
	    backend: CHECKIN_XP in checkinController.ts